From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] venc: take a new bit rate at a requested IDR

The rate control takes a changed bit rate (CVI_VENC_SetChnAttr) only on a
frame of an I period. cviCheckIdrPeriod computes is_i_period before a
requested IDR restarts the GOP, so that frame never counts, and every
requested IDR restarts the count toward the periodic one: with key frames
on request, a new bit rate never took effect. It now takes effect at a
requested IDR too, where the rate control starts over anyway. The read-only
module parameter nk_idr_bitrate tells user space.
---
--- a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/sample/main_enc_cvitest.c
+++ b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/vcodec/sample/main_enc_cvitest.c
@@ -114,6 +114,10 @@
 				 EncOpenParam *encOP, EncParam *encParam,
 				 Uint32 frameIdx, Uint32 fieldDone,
 				 int field_flag, vpu_buffer_t vbRoi); */
+/* Lets user space detect a driver that takes a new bit rate at a requested IDR. */
+static int nk_idr_bitrate = 1;
+module_param(nk_idr_bitrate, int, 0444);
+
 static void cviPicParamChangeCtrl(EncHandle handle, TestEncConfig *pEncConfig,
 				  EncOpenParam *pEncOP, EncParam *encParam,
 				  Uint32 frameIdx);
@@ -1713,8 +1717,10 @@
 			rateChangeCmd = TRUE;
 		}
 	} else {
-		// detect bitrate change
-		if (encParam->is_i_period &&
+		// detect bitrate change: at an I period, or at a requested IDR, which also restarts the GOP
+		// (cviCheckIdrPeriod ran before that restart, so is_i_period stays false on it). With IDRs
+		// on request only, a new bit rate otherwise never took effect.
+		if ((encParam->is_i_period || encParam->idr_request) &&
 		    pEncOP->bitRate != cviEncRc_GetParam(pRcInfo, E_BITRATE)) {
 			cviEncRc_SetParam(&handle->rcInfo, pEncOP, E_BITRATE);
 			rateChangeCmd = TRUE;
